<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Belisarius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 500–565</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Belisarius was the leading general of the Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-i">Justinian I</a>. He defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> at Dara in 530, helped crush the Nika riots in 532, destroyed the Vandal Kingdom in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> in 533–534 and led the long reconquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostrogoths">Ostrogoths</a>, taking Ravenna in 540. In old age he repelled the Kutrigur raid on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> in 559.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/belisarius.jpg" alt="Belisarius" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Petar Milošević · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Belisarius_mosaic.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
